    {
      "id": "M1hMyf1-YOtOR9kyJ1Tgh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -82.67885873270438,
      "y": -70.28571428571433,
      "width": 985.1390991210938,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EPCT5k0ZeqwvEmXVwe2EP"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6VZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1898065186,
      "version": 2695,
      "versionNonce": 1210506725,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791973777664,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In contrast to a user interface, which connects a computer to a person, an Application Programming \nInterface (API) connects computers or pieces of software to each other.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThere are different types of API:\n    - REST\n    - SOAP\n    - GraphQL\n    - gRPC\n    - WebSocket",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In contrast to a user interface, which connects a computer to a person, an Application Programming \nInterface (API) connects computers or pieces of software to each other.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThere are different types of API:\n    - REST\n    - SOAP\n    - GraphQL\n    - gRPC\n    - WebSocket",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "U_dUklzJoy_UuByxsjMr3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 172.56375135694225,
      "y": 196.64078204972407,
      "width": 749.3992309570312,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EPCT5k0ZeqwvEmXVwe2EP"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Vd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1190981858,
      "version": 2680,
      "versionNonce": 1471582969,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763628244857,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "APIs are intended to free the programmer from dealing with idiosyncrasies \nof different applications, and to provide software independence interactions.\n\nAn API works like a contract between systems: it defines what data or \nactions are available and how to request them, usually through structured \nformats such as JSON or XML. When one application calls an API, it sends \na request to a server, which processes the command and sends back a \nresponse. \nThis design allows software components and companies to work together.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "APIs are intended to free the programmer from dealing with idiosyncrasies \nof different applications, and to provide software independence interactions.\n\nAn API works like a contract between systems: it defines what data or \nactions are available and how to request them, usually through structured \nformats such as JSON or XML. When one application calls an API, it sends \na request to a server, which processes the command and sends back a \nresponse. \nThis design allows software components and companies to work together.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
