      "text": "1) Model architecture config (from HF)\n    - \"head_dim\": 128,\n    - \"hidden_size\": 3072,\n    - \"num_attention_heads\": 24,\n    - \"num_hidden_layers\": 28,\n    - \"num_key_value_heads\": 8,\n\n2) Bytes per token of KV cache \n\n    bytes_per_token = 2 x n_layers x (num_key_value_heads x head_dim) x bytes_per_element\n                          = 2 x 28 x (8 x 128) x 2 = 114688 bytes/token ≈ 0.114 MiB/tk\n\n3) Blocks pool on GPU\n    Available KV cache memory = 0.38 GiB = 380 MiB  --> GPU KV cache size =  380 / 0.114 ≈ 3300 tk\n\n4) Maximum concurrency | 500tk = 3,552 tk / 500 tk  ≈ 7x\n\nThe GPU KV cache size line reports the total number of tokens that can be stored in the GPU KV cache at once. \nThe Maximum concurrency line provides an estimate of how many requests can be served concurrently if each request \nrequires the specified number of tokens (500 in the example above). \n\nvLLM also provides comprehensive benchmarking tools for performance testing and evaluation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Model architecture config (from HF)\n    - \"head_dim\": 128,\n    - \"hidden_size\": 3072,\n    - \"num_attention_heads\": 24,\n    - \"num_hidden_layers\": 28,\n    - \"num_key_value_heads\": 8,\n\n2) Bytes per token of KV cache \n\n    bytes_per_token = 2 x n_layers x (num_key_value_heads x head_dim) x bytes_per_element\n                          = 2 x 28 x (8 x 128) x 2 = 114688 bytes/token ≈ 0.114 MiB/tk\n\n3) Blocks pool on GPU\n    Available KV cache memory = 0.38 GiB = 380 MiB  --> GPU KV cache size =  380 / 0.114 ≈ 3300 tk\n\n4) Maximum concurrency | 500tk = 3,552 tk / 500 tk  ≈ 7x\n\nThe GPU KV cache size line reports the total number of tokens that can be stored in the GPU KV cache at once. \nThe Maximum concurrency line provides an estimate of how many requests can be served concurrently if each request \nrequires the specified number of tokens (500 in the example above). \n\nvLLM also provides comprehensive benchmarking tools for performance testing and evaluation.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
